---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Influx Financial"
  description="How Influx Financial collects, uses, stores and discloses your personal information, and how to access or correct it."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  path="/privacy-policy"
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-07-01')}
>
  <p>
    <strong
      >[OWNER TO CONFIRM: This is a working draft. Have it reviewed and approved by your compliance
      adviser or lawyer before launch — privacy obligations for credit assistance providers include
      specific requirements this draft cannot verify.]</strong
    >
  </p>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} ("Influx", "we", "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This policy explains
    how we collect, use, store and disclose personal information in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988
    (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Through this website's enquiry forms we collect only the details you provide: your name, contact
    details, the service you're interested in, and your message. We deliberately do not collect tax
    file numbers, account numbers, identity documents or other sensitive financial information
    through website forms.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you become a client, we collect further information needed to provide credit assistance or
    accounting services — such as identification, income and expense details, assets and liabilities
    — directly from you and, with your consent, from third parties such as your employer, lenders
    and credit reporting bodies.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your enquiries and provide our services</li>
    <li>
      To assess your situation and provide credit assistance, including submitting applications to
      lenders with your consent
    </li>
    <li>To provide accounting and tax services through OneHQ Accounting, where you engage them</li>
    <li>To meet our legal and regulatory obligations</li>
    <li>With your consent, to keep in touch about your loans and reviews</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    We may disclose your information to lenders and their agents, valuers, insurers, our aggregator
    [OWNER TO CONFIRM: aggregator name], credit reporting bodies, and professional advisers — only
    as needed to provide our services or as required by law. We do not sell personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage and security</h2>
  <p>
    Information is stored in access-controlled systems. Website enquiries are transmitted over
    HTTPS. [OWNER TO CONFIRM: CRM/storage arrangements and whether any data is stored or processed
    overseas — disclosure of overseas recipients is required.]
  </p>

  <h2>Access and correction</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access to, or correction of, the personal information we hold about you by
    contacting us at <a href={site.contact.emailHref}>{site.contact.email}</a> or
    {site.contact.phone}.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe we have mishandled your information, contact us first — see our
    <a href="/complaints">complaints process</a>. If unresolved, you can contact the Office of the
    Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au).
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses only essential functionality and, where enabled, privacy-respecting analytics.
    [OWNER TO CONFIRM: analytics platform in use — update this section to match, and add a consent
    banner if a platform requiring consent is chosen.]
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
